.TH PAUSA 1 "2026-06-05" "pausa 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pausa \- full-screen terminal UI Pomodoro-style stopwatch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pausa
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pausa
is a full-screen terminal UI application that tracks daily study time with a
zero-starting counter, supports short and endless breaks, and renders a
GitHub-style heatmap calendar of study history. All data is stored locally in
SQLite.
.P
The interface is keyboard-driven. Focus is automatically managed by the
terminal; there is no mouse support.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Space
Start, pause, or resume the stopwatch.
.TP
.B b
Start a short break with a countdown timer.
.TP
.B B
Start an endless break (no countdown).
.TP
.B h
Toggle between the stopwatch view and the heatmap calendar.
.TP
.B r
Reset the stopwatch (requires confirmation with \fBy\fR or \fBn\fR).
.TP
.B y
Confirm the current prompt (e.g., reset confirmation).
.TP
.B n
Dismiss the current prompt.
.TP
.B q
Quit the application.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Quit the application.
.TP
.B Esc
Quit the application.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in a TOML file at
.IR ~/.config/pausa/config.toml .
If the file does not exist, defaults are written on first run.
.P
The following keys are supported:
.TP
.B short_break_minutes
Duration of the short break countdown in minutes (default: 10, must be > 0).
.TP
.B reset_time
Daily session reset time in HH:MM 24-hour format (default: "00:00").
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pausa/config.toml
Configuration file (TOML format).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pausa/pausa.db
SQLite database storing sessions and daily totals.
